    "locked": false,
    "maintainer_can_modify": true,
    "title": "wallet: reject duplicate inputs in sendall",
    "user": {
      "login": "Bruce039",
      "id": 109469941,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOBoZg9Q",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/109469941?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Bruce039",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "`sendall` with the `inputs` option doesn't check for duplicates. Each listed input is added to `total_input_value` in the loop at spend.cpp:1472, so passing the same UTXO twice counts its value twice.\n\nOn regtest, with a wallet that has a single 1 BTC UTXO:\n\n```\nsendall '[\"<addr>\"]' '{\"inputs\": [<utxo>, <utxo>]}'\n```\n\n- the RPC returns `complete: true`\n- the committed tx has 2 inputs (the same outpoint twice) and one output of 1.99998230 BTC\n- it isn't in the mempool, and `testmempoolaccept` rejects it with `bad-txns-inputs-duplicate`\n- after that, `listunspent` is empty and `getbalances` shows `nonmempool: -1.0` until the tx is abandoned\n\n`send` and `walletcreatefundedpsbt` aren't affected, because `CCoinControl::Select` removes duplicates.\n\nThis rejects a duplicated input with `Invalid parameter, duplicated input: <txid>:<vout>` (RPC_INVALID_PARAMETER). The message matches what `createrawtransaction` says for duplicated addresses. The new `sendall_fails_on_duplicate_input` test fails on master (\"No exception raised\") and passes with the fix. `wallet_send.py` still passes.\n",
